cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GRETEL in your research, please cite the framework paper below."
title: "GRETEL: Graph Counterfactual Explanation Evaluation Framework"
abstract: >-
  An open-source framework for developing and evaluating Graph Counterfactual
  Explanation methods. Datasets, machine learning models, explanation
  techniques and evaluation measures are pluggable components selected from a
  single configuration file, so methods from different papers can be compared
  under one protocol.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aiim-research/GRETEL"
url: "https://github.com/aiim-research/GRETEL/wiki"
keywords:
  - graph counterfactual explanations
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - graph neural networks
  - evaluation framework
  - reproducibility
